<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harald Bluetooth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 986</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Harald I of Denmark, Harald Gormsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harald Bluetooth was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from about 958 to about 986, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorm-the-old">Gorm the Old</a>. He accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> around 965 and raised the larger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jelling">Jelling</a> Stone, which claims that he won all Denmark and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> Christian. His reign saw the building of the Trelleborg ring fortresses. He was overthrown by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a> and died soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harald-bluetooth.jpg" alt="Harald Bluetooth" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anagoria · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1200_Harald_Bl%C3%A5tand_anagoria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
